{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791465103,"nonce":"Q6amr3FfN3aWLFuP9X7zIhia3FI=","title":"Validate event-driven Node host integration on Linux and Windows","message":"The macOS native host now sleeps through xwindow and coordinates libuv readiness without recurring window polling. Port/validate equivalent integration on the remaining desktop hosts before removing their 16 ms fallback. Linux can explore the pollable libuv backend descriptor and xwindow external-pump hooks; Windows needs appropriate IOCP/main-thread integration. Preserve timers, GPU futures, stdin/network/file events, pointer/keyboard/resize/close, multiple windows and HMR. Extend native-idle tests and measure zero idle polls plus near-zero process CPU on actual desktop backends. Follow-up to a31e4f0; macOS wake implementation is native/src/window_pump.rs.","files":null}]}